{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/resendownverification()"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"code":"POST \/api\/v1\/users\/me\/resend-verification","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (CONTRACT.md §25.1, §25.7) — resend the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"signed-in caller’s own"}]},{"type":"text","text":" verification mail, and say what happened."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/resendOwnVerification()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resendOwnVerification"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Takes no address. The server reads it off the caller’s own record, and this signature"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberately offers no way to name a different one: a parameter here would let an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authenticated session mail an arbitrary address."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlike "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/resendVerification(email:tenantID:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" this reports the outcome, because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"caller is signed in to the account it is asking about and none of the outcomes tells"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it anything it did not already bring with it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"returns — a token was minted and the mail ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"enqueued"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". Delivery is asynchronous","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and can still fail at the provider; a queue that accepts everything in front of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"provider that rejects it looks exactly like this succeeding (§25.7 rule 3).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AxiamError.authz","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (from ","type":"text"},{"code":"409","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — already verified, or an account state that must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not be sent a live token.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AxiamError.network","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (from ","type":"text"},{"code":"429","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — the daily resend limit.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"§25.7 rule 2 forbids falling back to the unauthenticated endpoint on either failure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and this SDK does not: that fallback turns both back into a silent success and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restores the bug this operation exists to fix, with an extra round trip.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Refused client-side with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no wire call","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" when there is no session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resendOwnVerification","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"AxiamSDK","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC21resendOwnVerificationyyYaKF","title":"resendOwnVerification()"},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient/resendVerification(email:tenantID:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/resendVerification(email:tenantID:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"resendVerification(email:tenantID:)","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/resendverification(email:tenantid:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"code":"POST \/api\/v1\/auth\/resend-verification","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (CONTRACT.md §25.1) — the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"unauthenticated","type":"text"}]},{"text":" resend, for a caller with no session.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resendVerification","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"email","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tenantID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient","title":"AxiamClient","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AxiamClient"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The AXIAM REST client (§1–§7, §9 of CONTRACT.md).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk